    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** The business faced continued top-line pressure as its paid member base contracted, but management pointed to an April uptick in paid active users as a potential sign of stabilization. Card-related monetization showed underlying strength, with interchange revenue expanding amid rising adoption of the corporate card and the open-card strategy. The ongoing migration to the New Expensify platform acts as a near-term drag, yet broad bank integrations and ecosystem development hint that a return to member growth could follow the transition.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership is steering a turnaround centered on the New Expensify rollout, deeper card monetization, and AI-driven features, while preserving positive free cash flow and reaffirming annual cash targets. An earnings miss and GAAP losses test credibility, but the April membership improvement and cash‑generating posture offer management an early proof point that the strategy is gaining traction.",
